BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU La Casa Latino Cultural Center
DTSTART:20261015T203000Z
DTEND:20261015T213000Z
LOCATION:INDIANA MEMORIAL UNION (UNION BUILDING)
GEO:39.167655;-86.523537
SUMMARY:Remembering the Climate Crisis
DESCRIPTION:Presentation Abstract: Minority groups are more vulnerable to
  the impacts of climate change than the rest of the population. Latinx pe
 ople are the largest growing minority in Indianapolis\, yet little is kno
 wn about how the local effects of climate change in the city impact this 
 population. In this talk\, Martell presents the preliminary findings of a
  study about how Latinx people in Indianapolis think about\, feel\, and r
 emember climate change as well as their reactions to it. The goal is to d
 evelop policy recommendations and provide insights for future educational
  interventions about climate change education and advocacy.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Presentation Abstract:</strong> M
 inority groups are more vulnerable to the impacts of climate change than 
 the rest of the population. Latinx people are the largest growing minorit
 y in Indianapolis\, yet little is known about how the local effects of cl
 imate change in the city impact this population. In this talk\, Martell p
 resents the preliminary findings of a study about how Latinx people in In
 dianapolis think about\, feel\, and remember climate change as well as th
 eir reactions to it. The goal is to develop policy recommendations and pr
 ovide insights for future educational interventions about climate change 
 education and advocacy.</p>
UID:20261015T203000Z-2442969@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20261007T115457Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2440335-remembering-the-climate-cri
 sis
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
LAST-MODIFIED:20261007T155457Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/363/width/168/height/168/crop
