 em><strong>About the CLACS Global Health Series</strong></em></p><p>  The
  CLACS Global Health Series brings together students\, faculty\, practiti
 oners\, and community members to explore health challenges and public hea
 lth initiatives across Latin America and the Caribbean. Developed in coor
 dination with <strong>Whitney Cordoba-Grueso</strong>\, MD\, PhD\, MPH\, 
 the series connects regional knowledge with interdisciplinary perspective
 s on global health\, including mental and reproductive health\, infectiou
 s and chronic disease\, migration\, environmental health\, and health equ
 ity.</p><p><em><strong>This event is free and open to everyone.</strong><
 /em> Students\, faculty\, staff\, and members of the wider community are 
 welcome.</p><p><strong>Planning to attend?</strong></p><p>  Please <a hre
 f="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1ELlf4f9KGCJBw8O8VT15om-_49sMXoYMXZAn0
 RDrCAA/edit"><span style="text-decoration: underline\;"><strong>register<
 /strong></span></a> using the button below. Registration is requested to 
 assist organizers with planning.</p>
